  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 144 PM EDT Sat Aug 15 2026\n\n\n- Chance of showers and isolated thunderstorms through Sunday\n\nLight showers are all that is currently moving through the region as\nquasi stationary front continues to keep a weakening MCV south of\nMichigan. The stable air over southern Michigan should continue \nto stifle convection. As a SFC low moves eastward this afternoon \nand evening it could move north enough to allow for scattered \nshowers and isolated storms along the I -94 corridor. The shear \nand CAPE remain through IN and Ohio so the threat of severe from \nany storms to forms continues to diminish. Any showers and storms \nthat form will be aided by the humid air mass and heavy rainfall \nwill be possible. \n\n  A short upper level wave and a deepening mid level trough will swing a \nfrontal system through the area tomorrow. This could allow for another chance  \nfor showers tomorrow morning into early afternoon. \n  While lapse rates aren't great and the front is coming at the wrong\ntime of day for convection, there should be sufficient CAPE and \nPWATS are upwards of 2 inches from latest CAMS. So any showers or\nstorms that do form could have periods of heavy rain. \n    \n- Drier and less humid through early part of week\n\n The front will move through tomorrow with cooler and drier air in \nits wake which will drop Temps and dewpoints down to normal making the\nare more comfortable. \n Max temperatures will be near normal, in the low 80s, through \nTuesday. \n\n\n- Another frontal system could bring showers and storms midweek\n\nThe quasi stationary high that was sitting over the south and allowed for \nall the weather to move through Illinois and Indiana this past week will\nshift to the west. \n  This upcoming week will be dominated by a large upper level low that will build over\nthe Hudson Bay. A it treks to the east will should move\nsouth over northern Ontario and a cold front extending from it should move\nfrom the northwest, across Michigan and sweep into the mid Atlantic \nby Thursday. \n There is some question on timing but currently, there is the \npotential for showers and storms Tuesday night into Wednesday. \nThis should also clear temperatures off for the latter half of \nthis upcoming week.",
